Title: Acceptance adapters pass the whole environment to sudo --preserve-env; sudo logs the values (HF_TOKEN in the journal)
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-11-09T13:12Z MinhHaDuong created
2026-11-09T15:30Z claude-sonnet-5-5 allowlist + wrap drop implemented; journal-line check not run (no live sudo allowed)
2026-11-09T16:29Z MinhHaDuong note verify-reroll — round 1: a posture run's sudo journal line lists only allowlisted names (unverified live); split to 0830 by the sprint lead, run.py follow-up filed as 0831

--- body ---
## Incident (2026-11-09, padme)
At 14:05:52 sudo logged, in padme's system journal (readable by the journal group), an
invocation as `untrusted-runner` from `/tmp/erg-roll/swz` whose `ENV=` list carried the whole
inherited environment, an `HF_TOKEN` value among it. The run was a `make check` by a harness
rollout agent (erg ID-claims migration). The posture probes just before passed only
`_ACCEPTANCE_POSTURE_PROBE`. Reported by the padme session; the value was not copied anywhere.
Rotating the token is the author's decision.

## Cause (from the source on origin/main)
`bench/acceptance/adapters/zotero_mcp.py:417` and `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py:430`
call `self._posture.wrap(cmd, {**os.environ, **env})`. `Posture.wrap`
(`bench/acceptance/posture.py:209-264`) turns every key into `sudo --preserve-env=<names>`.
Its docstring keeps values off argv, but sudo itself logs the preserved variables and their
values in its journal entry, so `--preserve-env` of the whole environment is the leak. The other
adapters pass `self.environment()` or a named `env` only.

## Fix wanted
- Never forward `os.environ` wholesale: pass an explicit allowlist of the names the target needs
  (as the other adapters do), in both adapters.
- Make `Posture.wrap` refuse (or drop with a warning) names that look like credentials
  (`*TOKEN*`, `*KEY*`, `*SECRET*`, `*PASSWORD*`) unless explicitly allowed, and update its
  docstring: sudo's own log is a channel too.
- A test that `wrap()` of a mapping containing `HF_TOKEN` does not put that name in
  `--preserve-env`, and that the two adapters build their env from an allowlist.

## Exit criteria
- [x] zotero_mcp.py and zoteus.py forward an explicit allowlist, not os.environ
- [x] wrap() never preserves a credential-looking name by default; docstring names sudo's log
- [x] tests cover both
- (moved to 0830 on 2026-11-09: a posture run's sudo journal line lists only allowlisted names; needs a live run on padme)
